\section{Masking}{

ggsaveR attaches ggplot2 when it is loaded, so \code{ggsaveR::ggsave()} masks
\code{ggplot2::ggsave()} regardless of the order of the \code{library()} calls. Use
\code{ggplot2::ggsave()} or \code{ggsave(..., guard = TRUE)} to reach the original.
}

